BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exploration of Forms: Divergent Rhythms with Alexis Riley — Berk
 eley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261011T110000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:46516a68529838a465523a7cbdb4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performing Arts\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United
  States
DESCRIPTION:This workshop offers an introduction to repetition as a disabi
 lity cultural movement practice. Inspired by (though in no way mimicking) 
 stimming and guided by an autistic artist\, this 90-minute session explore
 s iterative motion as an entry point into somatic exploration and movement
  improvisation. Everyone is welcome \, including autistic/neurodivergent\,
  mad/mentally ill\, and disabled people\, as well as others who are intere
 sted in respectfully engaging disability performance lineages in an access
 ible\, sensory-aware\, and beginner-friendly environment.\nCategory: Perfo
 rming Arts\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/33215
 3-exploration-of-forms-divergent-rhythms-with-alexis-ri
LOCATION:Bancroft Dance Studio\, 2401 Bancroft Way\, Bancroft Dance Studio
 \, 2401 Bancroft Way
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/332153-exploration-of-forms-div
 ergent-rhythms-with-alexis-ri
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
