CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:Interested in using interviews as part of your research? This 
 workshop series explores the relationship between oral history and researc
 h interviewing\, with an emphasis on thoughtful planning\, ethical practic
 e\, and responsible stewardship. Across three hands-on workshops\, partici
 pants will learn how to develop an interview project\, conduct research to
  prepare for an interview\, create effective questions\, establish rapport
 \, navigate consent and release forms\, and preserve interviews for future
  use. We’ll consider the different purposes interviews can serve\, from 
 documenting a person’s life story to exploring specific questions within
  a historical research project\, and examine examples from ac\nCategory: L
 ectures\, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.e
 du/library/event/337753-living-archives-an-oral-history-workshop-series-se
 ssi
