DESCRIPTION:A finalist for CrimeCon’s True Crime Book of the Year and wi
 nner of multiple literary awards\, Zenith Man\, updated now with new mater
 ial\, tells the extraordinary true story of Alvin Ridley\, a reclusive Geo
 rgia television repairman accused of murdering his wife after authorities 
 discovered a woman no one knew he had been married to. The case became a m
 edia sensation\, and nearly everyone assumed Ridley was guilty. As Ridley
 ’s defense attorney\, McCracken Poston uncovered a far more complex real
 ity. Years after Ridley’s acquittal\, Ridley was diagnosed with Autism S
 pectrum Disorder—a revelation that transformed understanding of both the
  man and the case. Behaviors once viewed as suspicious or incr\nCategory: 
 Books\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/an-evening-with-aut
 hor-mccracken-poston-on-zenith-man/
