CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Community Service\,Washington\, DC\,United Stat
 es
DESCRIPTION:Caregiving remains largely invisible\, uncompensated\, and und
 erappreciated\, even as demand outpaces the system. This session examines 
 the full caregiving continuum\, from family caregiving to the paid workfor
 ce\, tackling policy debates - paid leave\, respite care\, tax credits\, a
 nd direct pay models - alongside the collective response needed across hea
 lth care\, employers\, government\, and community. Speakers Amy Goyer - Na
 tional Family and Caregiving Expert\, AARP Ruth Kershner - National Family
  Caregiver Support Program\, Montgomery County DHHS Mary Lazare - Principa
 l Deputy Administrator\, Administration for Community Living (ACL) Tom Ste
 vens - Family caregiver\, former mayor\nCategory: Community Service\nOrigi
