DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:9ba8219c4306de344709dc0b1e17@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Representing the culmination of nearly a year of research by m
 ore than 20 GW students and alumni\, this symposium celebrates the launch 
 of an online exhibition dedicated to the print works of Marc Chagall in th
 e GW Collection. Although his achievements as an etcher are often eclipsed
  by his renowned paintings\, stained glass\, and monumental commissions\, 
 graphic art lies at the heart of his artistic practice. This online exhibi
 tion brings together 27 etchings from the GW Collection\, 14 of which are 
 from Nikolai Gogol’s Dead Souls \, and a unique silk scarf held by the G
 eorge Washington University Museum The Textile Museum. Beyond the works in
  the GW Collection\, Washington is home to numerous Cha\nCategory: Arts & 
 Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/hidden-treasures
 -of-chagall-in-washington-dc
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/hidden-treasures-of-chagall-in-washingt
 on-dc
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:America <-> Asia US-Taiwan Relations: Growing Strategic Convergenc
 e Faces Mutual Leadership Uncertainties — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261020T124500
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261020T134500
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:05ed938013c387aeaa799907ca39@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, Professor of Practice of International Affairs 
 Robert Sutter will explore the past\, present\, and future of the relation
 ship between the Republic of China (Taiwan) and the United States. He will
  begin by explaining the lasting legacies over the last 100 years of the R
 epublic of China government on Taiwan. Since the first Trump administratio
 n\, the US has hardened its policies and attitudes toward the People’s R
 epublic of China (China)\, with Taiwan playing a critical role in such a p
 olicy. However\, recently\, uncertainty has entered into the US-Taiwan rel
 ationship due to domestic and international headwinds. In Taiwan\, an upco
 ming 2028 presidential election could result in a dramat\nCategory: Academ
 ic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/america-asia-us-taiwa
 n-relations-growing-strategic-convergence-faces-mutual-leadership-uncertai
 nties
LOCATION:1957 E Street NW\, 1957 E St NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/america-asia-us-taiwan-relations-growin
 g-strategic-convergence-faces-mutual-leadership-uncertainties
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
