SUMMARY:A Gift in Motion — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T170000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:36ceab9489351e030d81a43bc938@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A multidisciplinary showcase from the artists and scholars of 
 the full-time faculty and staff at the Corcoran School of the Arts & Desig
 n. A Gift In Motion loosely draws from Robin Wall Kimmerer’s book The Se
 rviceberry which uplifts Indigenous frameworks of the natural world to adv
 ance the possibilities in collectivity\, reciprocity\, and the mindset of 
 abundance. These are anti-capitalist models and theories that provide insi
 ght into the systems of power we negotiate\, but also offer a lens on how 
 we individually move through our daily lives—together—through historic
 ally fraught landscapes. A keen reminder that working with\, for\, and bec
 ause of each other remains the most human motivation\, eve\nCategory: Arts
  & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/a-gift-in-mot
 ion
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/a-gift-in-motion
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cracks & Reforms: The 1920s Through the GW Collection — Washingt
 on\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261021T170000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:faeecaa418dc3843eb54b83d7193@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The 1920s emerged as a decade suspended between collapse and r
 econstruction\, an era marked by “cracks and reforms” that ushered in 
 a profound reconfiguration of the visual world.  During this period marke
 d by civil transformation and political upheaval\, artists\, journalists\,
  and makers had opportunities to reconstruct both individual and collectiv
 e identities. A century later\, Cracks & Reforms presents a distinct cross
 -section of this period\, revealing global currents of migration\, moderni
 zation\, and cultural redefinition through the lens of the GW Collection. 
 Students led by Associate Professor Bibiana Obler selected works to study 
 and exhibit\, their research eventually leading to unified t\nCategory: Ar
 ts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cracks-refo
 rms-the-1920s-through-the-gw-collection
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cracks-reforms-the-1920s-through-the-gw
 -collection
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
