SUMMARY:The Julian Clement Chase Prize Tenth Anniversary Celebration and A
 wards Ceremony — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261022T153000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261022T180000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:0e6a12d60657634ae1b8790bae53@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join the Julian Clement Chase Prize tenth anniversary celebrat
 ion featuring Maria Arana \, inaugural Literary Director of the Library of
  Congress\, and presentations by top student winners about places across D
 C : Malcolm X Park drum circles\, Mt. Zion cemetery in Georgetown\, Ethiop
 ian restaurants across DC over time\, and the Art Therapy program created 
 by GW students for elders with dementia at Residences at Thomas Circle. Th
 e Chase Prizes honor Sgt. Julian Clement Chase\, a Washington\, D.C. nativ
