SUMMARY:Statistics Seminar Series: Efficient and Stable Box-Cox Regression
  for High-Dimensional Data Analysis — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261023T140000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261023T150000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:f0820ae61edc16483fb5680aeca8@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Efficient and Stable Box-Cox Regression for High-Dimensional D
 ata Analysis Please join the Statistics Department for a talk featuring Hu
 i Zou\, professor in the Department of Applied Mathematics and Statistics 
 at Johns Hopkins University. The Box-Cox transformation paper ranks among 
 the five most-cited articles in the Journal of the Royal Statistical Socie
 ty\, Series B. Bickel and Doksum (1981) revisited this classical model thr
 ough analysis of the profile likelihood estimator and concluded that "the 
 performance of all Box-Cox type procedures is unstable." We argue\, howeve
 r\, that the scientific modeling philosophy of Box and Cox remains valuabl
 e in modern data analysis. To this end\, we develop\nCategory: Academic\nO
 riginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/statistics-seminar-series-
 efficient-and-stable-box-cox-regression-for-high-dimensional-data-analysis
LOCATION:Duques Hall\, 2201 G Street NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/statistics-seminar-series-efficient-and
 -stable-box-cox-regression-for-high-dimensional-data-analysis
