SUMMARY:Craft\, Conversation\, & Coffee: A Workshop on Legacy & Latch-Hook
  — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-04:00":20261024T120000
DTSTAMP:20261011T193532Z
UID:3507dea2c4f93c02ee3395dfb394@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:With Amanda Banks & Saudade Toxosi Coffee is one of the most t
 raded commodities in the world. Its supply chain touches nearly every cont
 inent and carries a long\, complicated history of land\, labor\, and extra
 ction. Artist Amanda Banks has spent time tracing her own family’s conne
 ction to that history. The burlap sacks she latch-hooks aren’t just recl
 aimed materials. They’re a way of working through what she’s learned\,
  stitch by stitch. In this hands-on workshop\, Banks will teach participan
 ts basic latch-hook techniques using reclaimed coffee sacks and recycled y
 arn. While you work\, she’ll share what she’s uncovered about her fami
 ly’s roots in the coffee industry and invite a broader conversat\nCatego
 ry: Art + Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/craft-co
 nversation-coffee-a-workshop-on-legacy-latch-hook/
LOCATION:Museum of Design Atlanta (MODA)\, 1315 Peachtree St. NE\, Atlanta
 \, GA\, 30309
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/craft-conversation-coffee-a-workshop-on-
 legacy-latch-hook/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
