CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:1998 | Run Time: 136 min. | 35mm Directed by Spike Lee Introdu
 ced by Dr. Samantha Sheppard (Cornell University) If you’ve ever watched
  New York professional basketball or witnessed the 2026 championship Knick
 s play\, you’ve seen Spike Lee live and in color. Lee is an avid basketb
 all fan and has floor seats for all Knicks home games. He is also the dire
 ctor of many commercials that illuminate the sport like Chic H.I.S.\, the 
 Continental Basketball Association\, and those that kicked off the relatio
 nship between Michael Jordan and Nike. Lee’s love and knowledge of baske
 tball make his 1998 film HE GOT GAME aesthetically beautiful and contempla
 tive. A fascinating look into one of America’s favorite\nCategory: Film 
 + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinematheq
 ue-presents-he-got-game-1998/
