 his month’s book club selection is Call Me Larry: A Creole Man’s Trium
 ph Over Racism and Homophobia by Larry Bagneris Jr. and Ryan Gomez \, a br
 acing\, uplifting\, and sometimes laugh-out-loud memoir in which Larry Bag
 neris recalls his activist career as founder of Houston’s Pride Parade a
 nd then\, following a return to his hometown\, as political organizer and 
